cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "StaticPE: a curated static-analysis benchmark for Windows PE malware"
message: "If you use this corpus, please cite the paper rather than the repository."
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Lachhab
    given-names: Aymane
    affiliation: "Sorbonne Universite, CNRS, LIP6"
  - family-names: Fossati
    given-names: Francesca
    affiliation: "Sorbonne Universite, CNRS, LIP6"
  - family-names: Liu
    given-names: Qiong
    affiliation: "Sorbonne Universite, CNRS, LIP6"
abstract: >-
  A benchmark of 100,909 Windows Portable Executable files, 83,885 malicious
  and 17,024 benign, extracted by a single chain into 18,489 usable columns
  with imported and exported functions kept under their full names. Every
  annotation records whether it was measured on the file or inherited from
  its family, and an unmeasured value is stored as null rather than folded
  into a measured zero. Five splitting policies are frozen in the released
  data: random, import-hash grouped, family grouped, out-of-time and
  cross-type.
keywords:
  - malware detection
  - static analysis
  - Portable Executable
  - dataset
  - splitting policy
  - data leakage
  - label provenance
license: CC-BY-4.0
